        skos:definition        "The physical parts of a cell including the cell wall (if present), cell membrane, nucleus, and other organelles."@en;
        skos:definition        "Les parties physiques d'une cellule, dont la paroi cellulaire (si présente), la membrane cellulaire, le noyau et les autres organites."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1280";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "structural cellular components"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "composants cellulaires structuraux"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1289/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1289";
        dc:date                "2025-08-07 11:06:05.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1289";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-08-07 11:06:05.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1289/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "A pincer-shaped organ at the end of certain limbs of some arthropods. It is typically formed by the articulation between the dactyl (movable finger) and the propodus (fixed finger), which together create a grasping structure."@en;
        skos:definition        "Organe en forme de pince à l'extrémité de certains appendices de quelques arthropodes. Il est généralement formé par l'articulation entre le dactyle (doigt mobile) et le propode (doigt fixe), qui forment ensemble une structure de préhension."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1289";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "chela"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "chéla"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1269/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1269";
        dc:date                "2021-07-07 09:41:12.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1269";
        pav:authoredOn         "2021-07-07 09:41:12.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1269/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The upper part of an organism's two-part beak or beak-like projecting structure. The term is used in reference to cetaceans, crustaceans, cephalopods and some fishes."@en;
        skos:definition        "Partie supérieure du bec bipartite d'un organisme ou de la structure saillante en forme de bec. Le terme s'applique aux cétacés, crustacés, céphalopodes et certains poissons."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1269";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "upper rostrum"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "rostre supérieur"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S12100/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S12100";
        dc:date                "2025-12-19 11:37:03.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S12100";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-12-19 11:37:03.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S12100/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "An elongated appendage from the head or mouth region of an organism. In invertebrates the proboscis is typically a tubular feeding or sucking organ but it can also be involved in the capture of prey or locomotion. In some invertebrates such as the Class Enteropneusta (acorn worms) the proboscis is the anteriormost of three body regions. In vertebrates the term typically refers to an elongated nose, snout, or trunk."@en;
        skos:definition        "Appendice allongé issu de la tête ou de la région buccale d'un organisme. Chez les invertébrés, la trompe est généralement un organe tubulaire d'alimentation ou de succion, mais elle peut aussi participer à la capture des proies ou à la locomotion. Chez certains invertébrés comme la classe des Enteropneusta (vers à glands), la trompe est la plus antérieure des trois régions du corps. Chez les vertébrés, le terme désigne généralement un nez, un museau ou une trompe allongée."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S12100";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "proboscis"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "trompe"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1298/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1298";
        dc:date                "2025-12-12 10:28:05.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1298";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-12-12 10:28:05.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1298/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "VRM";
        skos:altLabel          "VRM"@fr ;
        skos:definition        "A longitudinal muscle located along the ventral body wall of certain invertebrates, responsible for retracting anterior structures such as the introvert or proboscis toward the ventral side of the trunk. It typically originates on the ventral internal body wall and inserts on the anterior organ or structure it retracts."@en;
        skos:definition        "Muscle longitudinal situé le long de la paroi ventrale du corps de certains invertébrés, responsable de la rétraction des structures antérieures comme l'introvert ou la trompe vers la face ventrale du tronc. Il prend généralement origine sur la paroi interne ventrale et s'insère sur l'organe ou la structure antérieure qu'il rétracte."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1298";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ventral retractor muscle"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "muscle rétracteur ventral"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1293/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1293";
        dc:date                "2025-11-07 10:39:00.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1293";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-11-07 10:39:00.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1293/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "In invertebrates, the abdomen is the posterior body segment that contains most of the digestive and reproductive organs. The vertebrate abdomen is the body cavity located behind the ribcage and in front of the pelvic cavity, enclosed by muscles and the vertebral column. It contains vital organs from systems like the digestive (e.g. stomach, intestines), urinary, and others, which are protected by the abdominal muscles and separated from the thoracic cavity by the diaphragm."@en;
        skos:definition        "Chez les invertébrés, l'abdomen est le segment postérieur du corps qui contient la plupart des organes digestifs et reproducteurs. L'abdomen vertébré est la cavité corporelle située derrière la cage thoracique et devant la cavité pelvienne, entourée de muscles et de la colonne vertébrale. Il contient des organes vitaux de systèmes comme le système digestif (estomac, intestins), urinaire et d'autres, protégés par les muscles abdominaux et séparés de la cavité thoracique par le diaphragme."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1293";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "abdomen"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "abdomen"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1290/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1290";
        dc:date                "2025-08-07 11:06:17.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1290";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-08-07 11:06:17.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1290/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "A sharp usually slender and curved nail or extension at the end of a toe or limb in some organisms, or one of the pincer-like organs on some limbs of arthropods."@en;
        skos:definition        "Griffe ou prolongement pointu, généralement fin et courbé, à l'extrémité d'un orteil ou d'un appendice chez certains organismes, ou l'un des organes en forme de pince sur certains appendices des arthropodes."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1290";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "claw"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "griffe"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S12102/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S12102";
        dc:date                "2026-02-19 10:57:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S12102";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-02-19 10:57:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S12102/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "A muscular, internal organ within the digestive system that receives ingested food and begins its breakdown through mechanical processing and chemical digestion, typically using acids and enzymes."@en;
        skos:definition        "Organe interne musculaire du système digestif qui reçoit les aliments ingérés et amorce leur dégradation par traitement mécanique et digestion chimique, généralement à l'aide d'acides et d'enzymes."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S12102";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "stomach"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "estomac"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1271/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1271";
        dc:date                "2021-07-07 09:41:15.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1271";
        pav:authoredOn         "2021-07-07 09:41:15.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1271/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The anterior of the two or three main divisions of the body of certain invertebrates."@en;
        skos:definition        "La partie antérieure des deux ou trois divisions principales du corps de certains invertébrés."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1271";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "prosome"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "prosome"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1279/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1279";
        dc:date                "2022-05-13 10:09:32.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1279";
        pav:authoredOn         "2022-05-13 10:09:32.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1279/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The underground structures of a plant including the rhizomes which are subterranean horizontal stems from which roots and shoots can grow; and roots which are the parts of a plant which attach it to the ground or to a support, typically underground, conveying water and nourishment to the rest of the plant via numerous branches and fibres."@en;
        skos:definition        "Les structures souterraines d'une plante, dont les rhizomes qui sont des tiges horizontales souterraines d'où peuvent pousser racines et pousses ; et les racines, parties de la plante qui l'ancrent au sol ou à un support, généralement sous terre, et qui conduisent eau et nutriments au reste de la plante via de nombreuses ramifications et fibres."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1279";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "roots+rhizomes"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "racines+rhizomes"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1268/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1268";
        dc:date                "2021-07-07 09:41:10.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1268";
        pav:authoredOn         "2021-07-07 09:41:10.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1268/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The lower part of an organism's two-part beak or beak-like projecting structure. The term is used in reference to cetaceans, crustaceans, cephalopods and some fishes."@en;
        skos:definition        "Partie inférieure du bec bipartite d'un organisme ou de la structure saillante en forme de bec. Le terme s'applique aux cétacés, crustacés, céphalopodes et certains poissons."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1268";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "lower rostrum"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "rostre inférieur"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1262/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1262";
        dc:date                "2021-07-07 09:54:22.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1262";
        pav:authoredOn         "2021-07-07 09:54:22.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1262/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1262/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Also called pallium, plural pallia, or palliums, in biology, a soft covering, formed from the body wall, of brachiopods and molluscs; also, the fleshy outer covering, sometimes strengthened by calcified plates, of barnacles. (www.britannica.com)"@en;
        skos:definition        "Aussi appelé pallium (pluriel : pallia, palliums), en biologie, enveloppe molle formée par la paroi du corps des brachiopodes et des mollusques ; aussi, l'enveloppe externe charnue, parfois renforcée par des plaques calcifiées, des cirripèdes. (www.britannica.com)"@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1262";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mantle"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "manteau"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1286/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1286";
        dc:date                "2024-02-01 16:38:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1286";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-02-01 16:38:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1286/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The stalk or stem of plants (including macroalgae) and fungi."@en;
        skos:definition        "La tige ou le stipe des plantes (y compris les macroalgues) et des champignons."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1286";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "stipe"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "stipe"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1295/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1295";
        dc:date                "2025-12-12 10:25:37.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1295";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-12-12 10:25:37.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1295/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The main section of the body of an animal, excluding the head, neck, and limbs/tail. In Sipuncula this is the larger, unsegmented, and typically bulbous posterior portion of the worm's body into which its narrower anterior section, the introvert, can be fully retracted."@en;
        skos:definition        "La section principale du corps d'un animal, excluant la tête, le cou et les membres/la queue. Chez les Sipuncula, il s'agit de la portion postérieure plus large, non segmentée et généralement bulbeuse du corps du ver, dans laquelle sa section antérieure plus étroite, l'introvert, peut se rétracter entièrement."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1295";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "trunk region"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "région du tronc"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1275/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1275";
        dc:date                "2021-08-25 08:28:39.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1275";
        pav:authoredOn         "2021-08-25 08:28:39.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1275/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The central body part of a starfish (Asteroidea) also known as sea star, containing the internal organs, and the mouth and anus, and from which arms arms radiate. The radius of the central disc is used as a standard biometric measurement in starfish studies."@en;
        skos:definition        "La partie centrale du corps d'une étoile de mer (Asteroidea), contenant les organes internes ainsi que la bouche et l'anus, et d'où rayonnent les bras. Le rayon du disque central est utilisé comme mesure biométrique standard dans les études sur les étoiles de mer."@fr ;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S12::S1275";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "central disc"@en ;
        skos:prefLabel         "disque central"@fr .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S12/current/S1288/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:S12::S1288";
        dc:date                "2025-08-07 11:06:04.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:S12::S1288";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-08-07 11:06:04.0";
